<section class="about-how">
    <div class="about-how-inner">
        <h2 class="about-how-title">How does it work?</h2>
        <div class="about-how-columns">
            <div class="about-how-column">
                <h3 class="about-how-column-title">How does the Learning Hub work?</h3>
                <div class="about-how-text">
                    <p>
                        Resources are organised around 10 thematic areas, formats and tags, helping people navigate topics, discover connections and follow their curiosity.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        At its core, the methodology sees learning as an open and evolving process in which knowledge is developed through practice and strengthened through exchange. Rather than offering a fixed learning path, the Learning Hub allows everyone to explore at their own pace, combining resources and experiences according to their interests and needs. By encouraging people to adapt knowledge to their own contexts and put it into practice, the Learning Hub supports the development of approaches and activities that can be shared, replicated and further adapted by others.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="about-how-column">
                <h3 class="about-how-column-title">How does LLM work?</h3>
                <div class="about-how-text">
                    <p>
                        The Learning Hub brings together original resources, knowledge and materials contributed by its community. To make this collection easier to explore, we developed a dedicated Large Language Model (LLM) system that automatically generates topic-based summaries using only the content available on the platform.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        For example, when searching for a topic such as biomaterials, the system analyses relevant resources in the Learning Hub and generates an overview to introduce the subject and point you towards useful materials. It can be considered a starting point for discovery; summaries help you navigate the collection, but do not replace the original resources or expertise behind them.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <a class="about-how-link" href="{{ url_for('about_llms') }}">
                    Learn more about our use of LLM
